{
 "cells": [
  {"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{},"source":["# JAK2 V617F Molecular Analysis\n","\n","**End-to-end reproducible case study:** reference-sequence retrieval → codon extraction → in-silico G>T substitution → translation → variant annotation → molecular interpretation.\n","\n","Canonical variant: **NM_004972.4:c.1849G>T → p.Val617Phe (V617F)**; dbSNP **rs77375493**; GRCh38 **NC_000009.12:g.5073770G>T**.\n","\n","> Educational/research workflow; not a clinical diagnostic assay."]},
  {"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{},"source":["## 1. Objectives\n","\n","1. Retrieve the authoritative JAK2 RefSeq transcript at runtime.\n","2. Locate coding position c.1849 and extract the affected codon.\n","3. Introduce the G>T substitution computationally.\n","4. Translate reference and alternate codons and verify Val→Phe.\n","5. Create a machine-readable annotation/evidence table.\n","6. Produce a publication-style molecular consequence figure.\n","7. Preserve provenance and reproducibility information."]},
  {"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{},"outputs":[],"source":["from pathlib import Path\n","import sys\n","import pandas as pd\n","import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n\n","ROOT = Path.cwd().parent if Path.cwd().name == 'analysis' else Path.cwd()\nsys.path.insert(0, str(ROOT / 'scripts'))\nfrom reference_sequence_analysis import analyze_codon, fetch_fasta, parse_fasta, ACCESSION\n"]},
  {"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{},"source":["## 2. Canonical variant record"]},
  {"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{},"outputs":[],"source":["variant = pd.DataFrame([{\n","    'Gene': 'JAK2',\n","    'Transcript': ACCESSION,\n","    'HGVS_c': 'NM_004972.4:c.1849G>T',\n","    'HGVS_p': 'p.Val617Phe',\n","    'dbSNP': 'rs77375493',\n","    'Assembly': 'GRCh38',\n","    'Genomic_HGVS': 'NC_000009.12:g.5073770G>T',\n","    'Domain': 'JH2 pseudokinase domain'\n","}])\n","variant.T.rename(columns={0: 'Value'})\n"]},
  {"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{},"source":["## 3. Retrieve and verify the reference sequence\n","\n","The analysis engine retrieves **NM_004972.4** from NCBI at runtime. This keeps the reference sequence external and versioned rather than silently embedding a copied sequence in the repository."]},
  {"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{},"outputs":[],"source":["fasta = fetch_fasta()\n","sequence = parse_fasta(fasta)\n","print(f'Retrieved {ACCESSION}: {len(sequence):,} nucleotides')\n"]},
  {"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{},"outputs":[],"source":["result = analyze_codon(sequence)\n","pd.Series(result)\n"]},
  {"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{},"source":["## 4. Sequence-level consequence\n","\n","The engine verifies the reference nucleotide at c.1849, extracts c.1849–c.1851, substitutes T for G, and translates the two codons using the standard genetic code."]},
  {"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{},"outputs":[],"source":["assert result['hgvs_c'] == 'NM_004972.4:c.1849G>T'\n","assert result['reference_amino_acid'] == 'V'\n","assert result['alternate_amino_acid'] == 'F'\n","assert result['hgvs_p'] == 'p.Val617Phe'\n\n","consequence = pd.DataFrame([\n","    ['cDNA', result['reference_codon'][0], result['alternate_codon'][0], 'c.1849G>T'],\n","    ['Codon', result['reference_codon'], result['alternate_codon'], 'codon 617'],\n","    ['Protein', 'Valine (V)', 'Phenylalanine (F)', 'p.Val617Phe'],\n"], columns=['Level','Reference','Alternate','Interpretation'])\n","consequence\n"]},
  {"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{},"source":["## 5. Molecular interpretation pathway"]},
  {"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{},"outputs":[],"source":["steps = ['JAK2\nreference', 'c.1849G>T', 'p.Val617Phe', 'JH2\npseudokinase domain', 'JAK-STAT\ndysregulation', 'MPN\ncontext']\n","fig, ax = plt.subplots(figsize=(12, 3.2))\n","x = range(len(steps))\n","ax.plot(x, [0]*len(steps), marker='o', linewidth=2)\n","for i, step in enumerate(steps):\n","    ax.text(i, 0.08, step, ha='center', va='bottom', fontsize=9)\n","    if i < len(steps)-1:\n","        ax.annotate('', xy=(i+0.78, 0), xytext=(i+0.22, 0), arrowprops={'arrowstyle':'->','lw':1.2})\n","ax.set_xlim(-0.4, len(steps)-0.6)\n","ax.set_ylim(-0.35, 0.45)\n","ax.axis('off')\n","ax.set_title('JAK2 V617F: molecular consequence to biological context', fontsize=13, pad=14)\n","plt.tight_layout()\n","plt.show()\n"]},
  {"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{},"source":["## 6. Diagnostic context\n","\n","JAK2 V617F is an important molecular marker in classical BCR::ABL1-negative MPNs. A molecular result should be integrated with CBC findings, peripheral-blood and bone-marrow morphology, clinical findings, and other molecular drivers such as **CALR** and **MPL** when appropriate. A negative JAK2 V617F result does not by itself exclude an MPN.\n","\n","Database classifications should be interpreted in the appropriate disease and variant-origin context; somatic MPN evidence should not be conflated with germline variant interpretation."]},
  {"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{},"outputs":[],"source":["diagnostic_framework = pd.DataFrame({\n","    'Stage': ['Clinical assessment','Hematology','Molecular testing','Bioinformatics','Integrated interpretation'],\n","    'Examples': ['Symptoms and examination','CBC + morphology','JAK2 V617F / CALR / MPL','HGVS + annotation + QC','Clinical + laboratory + molecular evidence']\n","})\n","diagnostic_framework\n"]},
  {"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{},"source":["## 7. Reproducibility and provenance\n","\n","Record the reference accession/version, genome assembly, database releases, software versions, parameters, generated outputs, and repository commit. The live NCBI retrieval step is separated from deterministic unit tests so CI can remain independent of external network availability."]},
  {"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{},"outputs":[],"source":["provenance = {\n","    'reference_transcript': ACCESSION,\n","    'hgvs_c': result['hgvs_c'],\n","    'hgvs_p': result['hgvs_p'],\n","    'dbsnp': 'rs77375493',\n","    'assembly': 'GRCh38',\n","    'analysis_status': 'PASS: canonical nucleotide-to-protein consequence verified'\n","}\n","pd.Series(provenance)\n"]},
  {"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{},"source":["## 8. Conclusion\n","\n","This notebook demonstrates an end-to-end computational chain from a versioned JAK2 reference transcript to the canonical V617F protein consequence and its molecular diagnostic context. It is designed to be inspectable, reproducible, testable, and extensible to CALR, MPL and broader MPN variant workflows."]}
